v><p class="max-w-xl text-sm leading-6 text-white/70">Metrics below are limited to values that can be directly supported by the supplied 2024-2026 source document.</p></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5"><div class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5 backdrop-blur"><p class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">8</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white/75">Implementation states named in Year 2 progress</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5 backdrop-blur"><p class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">6</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white/75">Official SAS-CAP objectives</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5 backdrop-blur"><p class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">46</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white/75">2024-2026 scientific outputs listed in the source document</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5 backdrop-blur"><p class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">26</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white/75">Year 1 outreach and Extension records summarized</p></div><div class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5 backdrop-blur"><p class="text-3xl font-semibold text-white">4</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white/75">Undergraduate trainees noted in Year 2 workforce development</p></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-white py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between"><div class="max-w-3xl"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-700">Research Highlights</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-cotton-900 sm:text-4xl">Selected areas of emphasis</h2><p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-cotton-900/70">Explore core research themes shaping the project, from soil carbon and greenhouse gas measurement to precision management and production resilience.</p></div><a class="focus-ring inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md text-sm font-semibold text-skydata-700 underline" href="/smartcotton-website/research-highlights">View all highlights<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="group rounded-lg border border-cotton-200/80 bg-white/95 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-cotton-300 hover:shadow-soft"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-skydata-700">Soil systems</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Soil Carbon, Soil Health, and Carbon-Intensity Baselines</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">SmartCotton teams are collecting and analyzing soil organic carbon, carbon and nitrogen profiles, soil respiration, wet aggregate stability, AMF, phosphatase activity, and related soil health indicators across Cotton Belt environments.</p><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/65">Year 2 included Texas sampling across five tillage and cover crop treatments, New Mexico soil profile carbon and nitrogen work, Georgia and North Carolina SOC and AMF sampling, and Mississippi completion of 30 on-farm soil sampling sites.</p></div></article><article class="group rounded-lg border border-cotton-200/80 bg-white/95 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-cotton-300 hover:shadow-soft"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-skydata-700">Regenerative systems</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Cover Crops, Tillage, Bed Systems, and Regenerative Cotton</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">Field research evaluates cover crops, reduced tillage, raised and flat bed systems, cotton/forage sorghum rotation, irrigated desert production, and organic or transitional practices.</p><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/65">Preliminary Texas Blackland results showed cover crops maintained or improved yield performance, especially under the two-week termination treatment. Arizona cover crop treatments produced higher lint yield than controls under irrigated conditions.</p></div></article><article class="group rounded-lg border border-cotton-200/80 bg-white/95 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-cotton-300 hover:shadow-soft"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-skydata-700">Regenerative systems</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Living Mulches, Weed Suppression, and Cotton Root Traits</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">Teams are studying cool-season perennial grasses, weed suppression, allelopathic cotton lines, cereal rye termination, cotton root traits, and photosynthetic traits in regenerative systems.</p><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/65">Year 2 outputs included WSSA, Southern Cover Crop Council, Southern Weed Science Society, Beltwide, and CANVAS presentations on living mulches, cover crop termination, root traits, NDVI, and weed suppression.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="border-y border-cotton-200 bg-cotton-50 py-16 md:py-20"><div class="container-page"><div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between"><div class="max-w-3xl"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-700">Annual Progress</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-cotton-900 sm:text-4xl">Year 1 and Year 2 progress at a glance</h2><p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-cotton-900/70">Concise public summaries connect launch-year outreach and outputs with Year 2 objective-wise research, economics, adoption, Extension, and training progress.</p></div><a class="focus-ring inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md text-sm font-semibold text-skydata-700 underline" href="/smartcotton-website/publications#annual-reports">View report library<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="group rounded-lg border border-cotton-200/80 bg-white/95 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-cotton-300 hover:shadow-soft"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-skydata-700">Year 1 | 2024-2025</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Launch-year outputs, outreach, and foundational engagement</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">The Year 1 source content documents the official project objectives, initial scientific outputs, early regenerative cotton research dissemination, and a broad outreach/Extension program from June 2024 through February 2025.</p><div class="mt-5"><div class="grid gap-2 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70"><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 1<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->Early regenerative cotton and soil health outputs</p><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 1<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->Hyphosphere and soil microbiome method development</p><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 5<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->Outreach and Extension across grower, consultant, and industry audiences</p></div><a class="focus-ring mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-sm text-sm font-semibold text-skydata-700 underline" href="/smartcotton-website/reports/smartcotton-2024-2025-report.pdf"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-file-down" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7Z"></path><path d="M14 2v4a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h4"></path><path d="M12 18v-6"></path><path d="m9 15 3 3 3-3"></path></svg>Download report PDF</a></div></article><article class="group rounded-lg border border-cotton-200/80 bg-white/95 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-cotton-300 hover:shadow-soft"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-skydata-700">Year 2 | 2025-2026</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Expanded field research, datasets, economics, adoption, Extension, and training</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">Year 2 progress advanced multi-state field research, soil and microbial analyses, regenerative practice evaluation, precision technology development, economic analysis, farmer adoption studies, outreach, and workforce development across Texas, New Mexico, Arizona, Georgia, North Carolina, Mississippi, Alabama, and Tennessee.</p><div class="mt-5"><div class="grid gap-2 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70"><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 1<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->Regenerative production systems and soil health measurements</p><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 2<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->AI/ML-ready datasets and simulation-based decision support</p><p><span class="font-semibold text-cotton-900">Objective 3<!-- -->:</span> <!-- -->Economics, profitability, risk, and market potential</p></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-cotton-900/70">Pending approved report file</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="bg-cotton-900 py-20 text-white"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-4xl"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Project Goals</p><h2 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Six official objectives guide the SAS-CAP work.</h2><p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-white/75">The project links regenerative production, precision technologies, economics, adoption research, outreach, and education so Cotton Belt findings can move from experiments into practical decision-making.</p></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->1</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Regenerative production practices and long-term effects</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Develop regenerative cotton production practices and investigate their long-term effects on U.S. Cotton Belt production systems.</p></article><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->2</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Precision AI/ML and smart technologies</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Develop and/or evaluate precision AI/ML and smart technologies for resource conservation and climate-change mitigation and adaptation in cotton.</p></article><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->3</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Economic feasibility and market opportunities</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Evaluate economic feasibility of precision regenerative production practices and determine new market opportunities.</p></article><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->4</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Farmer adoption experiences</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Understand farmers&#x27; multidimensional experiences and adoption of regenerative practices across the Cotton Belt.</p></article><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->5</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Extension and outreach</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Promote adoption of regenerative climate-smart cotton practices through innovative and collaborative Extension and outreach activities.</p></article><article class="rounded-lg border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-5"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-200">Objective <!-- -->6</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-6 text-white">Education and rural workforce development</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-white/75">Provide educational opportunities for the next generation of research and Extension scientists and practitioners and strengthen rural workforce development.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="bg-white py-24"><div class="container-page grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="border-t border-cotton-200 pt-6"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Latest News</h2><a class="focus-ring rounded-sm text-sm font-semibold text-skydata-700 underline" href="/smartcotton-website/news">All news</a></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-cotton-900">Year 2 progress expands SmartCotton research across eight states</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">The project advanced multi-state field research, soil and microbial analyses, regenerative practice evaluation, precision technology planning, economic analysis, farmer adoption studies, outreach, and training across Texas, New Mexico, Arizona, Georgia, North Carolina, Mississippi, Alabama, and Tennessee.</p></div><div class="border-t border-cotton-200 pt-6"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Upcoming Event</h2><a class="focus-ring rounded-sm text-sm font-semibold text-skydata-700 underline" href="/smartcotton-website/events">All events</a></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-cotton-900">Cotton Cropping Systems Field Day</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">The source document lists a field day with nearly 100 attendees and a research stop on cotton cropping systems evaluated in the SAS project.</p></div></div></section><section class="bg-cotton-50 py-20"><div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between"><div><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-700">Partners</p><h2 class="mt-2 max-w-2xl font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Built for a multi-institutional cotton research network.</h2></div><p class="max-w-xl text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">SmartCotton is built through collaboration among universities, extension programs, growers, and industry partners working across major cotton production regions.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white py-20"><div class="container-page"><div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between"><div><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-cotton-700">Contact</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-cotton-900">Connect with the SmartCotton project</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-cotton-900/70">Contact the project team for research questions, outreach coordination, publication requests, and partnership opportunities.</p></div><a class="focus-ring inli